    rn: "Monitor TSH. Check heart rate and BP before starting; watch for toxicity (hyperthyroid signs). Monitor growth in children. Administration: PO on an empty stomach with a full glass of water, 30–60 minutes before breakfast; IV form reconstituted with NS. Separate from antacids, calcium, iron, PPIs, sucralfate, and bile acid sequestrants. Increases warfarin's effect; insulin needs may rise.",
    teach: "Take every morning at the same time, 30 to 60 minutes before breakfast, on an empty stomach. Treatment is lifelong; don't stop. Report signs of too much (fast heartbeat, chest pain, heat intolerance, nervousness, weight loss) or too little (fatigue, cold intolerance, weight gain). Tell the provider about pregnancy.",
