    rn: "Assess for manifestations of hypo- and hyperthyroidism, thyrotoxicosis, and thyroid storm. Monitor thyroid function and WBC with differential. Watch for rash, swelling, and lymphadenopathy. Administration: same time each day, consistently with or without food. Amiodarone and potassium iodide reduce its effect.",
    teach: "Report sore throat, fever, chills, mouth sores, or malaise right away (agranulocytosis). Weigh yourself two to three times a week. Report signs of too low or too high thyroid. Be cautious with iodine intake. Tell the provider about planned pregnancy.",
