    rn: "Monitor for neurotoxicity: paresthesia, loss of deep tendon reflexes. Monitor counts for leukopenia and thrombocytopenia. Check vital signs and the IV site for extravasation. Administration: IV only, as a 10–15 minute mini-bag infusion or IV push over 1 minute.",
    teach: "Report numbness, tingling, weakness, or constipation right away. Avoid crowds and wash hands often. Use contraception during and for 2 months after treatment.",
